WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.305
A tarot spread is a set of cards laid out in a pattern, where
each position in the pattern asks its own question.

00:00:09.605 --> 00:00:11.640
Cards, positions and a question.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.611
A tarot spread has three parts.

00:00:13.611 --> 00:00:17.616
There are the cards themselves, which come
from a 78-card deck.

00:00:18.916 --> 00:00:21.430
How a spread differs from a single draw.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.571
Drawing one card is the simplest way to
use tarot.

00:00:24.571 --> 00:00:28.970
You ask a question, turn over a card and
think about what it suggests.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:32.648
Have a tarot spread in front of you?

00:00:32.648 --> 00:00:37.266
Photograph it at readmyspread.com, and get
a clear reading, card by card.
